{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWWygM6M8zt8Asoi4MyW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QSBTNJFEFo4ohcfmkL1q4e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/BLAST_RADIUS.md","content":"# CVE Blast Radius Analysis: lodash Command Injection\n\n## 1. CVE Identification\n\n- **CVE ID:** CVE-2021-23337\n- **Affected package:** `lodash` (npm)\n- **Vulnerability class:** Command Injection / arbitrary code execution via `_.template`\n- **Root cause:** Insufficient sanitization of the template source string allowed the `_.template` function's generated function body to escape the intended sandbox via the Node.js `Function` constructor, allowing an attacker who controls the template string to execute arbitrary JavaScript.\n- **Vulnerable version range:** `< 4.17.21`\n- **Fixed version:** `4.17.21`\n- **Advisory:** GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm\n\nThis maps 1:1 onto the local `lodash` repo mirror: `/workspace/lodash/package.json` declares:\n\n```json\n\"name\": \"lodash\",\n\"version\": \"4.17.20\"\n```\n\n`/workspace/lodash` at version **4.17.20 is itself inside the vulnerable range** — it predates the 4.17.21 fix.\n\n## 2. Direct Dependents\n\nRepos/manifests in the workspace that declare a direct dependency on `lodash` (or `lodash-es`):\n\n| Repo | Manifest | Field | Declared range |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| webpack | `/workspace/webpack/package.json` (line 80) | `devDependencies.lodash` | `^4.17.19` |\n| webpack | `/workspace/webpack/package.json` (line 81) | `devDependencies[\"lodash-es\"]` | `^4.17.15` |\n| webpack | `/workspace/webpack/package.json` (line 46) | `devDependencies.benchmark` (transitively requires lodash — see §3) | `^2.1.4` |\n| jest | `/workspace/jest/examples/manual-mocks/package.json` (line 15) | `dependencies.lodash` | `^4.17.19` |\n\nNotes:\n- No package under `/workspace/jest/packages/*` (the actual jest workspace members — `jest-haste-map`, `jest-resolve`, `jest-runtime`, etc.) declares a direct dependency on `lodash`. The only direct, first-party reference inside the jest repo is the standalone example at `/workspace/jest/examples/manual-mocks/package.json`, which is **not** part of the jest yarn workspace (`workspaces: [\"packages/*\"]` in `/workspace/jest/package.json`, line 119-120) and has **no lockfile of its own**.\n- webpack is a single-package repo (not a monorepo), so its one root `/workspace/webpack/package.json` is the only manifest that can declare a direct dependency.\n\n## 3. Transitive Paths\n\n### webpack (`/workspace/webpack/`)\n\nTraced via `/workspace/webpack/yarn.lock` (classic yarn v1 lockfile):\n\n1. `webpack` → `lodash` *(direct, devDependency)* — 1 hop\n2. `webpack` → `lodash-es` *(direct, devDependency)* — 1 hop\n3. `webpack` → `benchmark` (`^2.1.4`, direct devDependency) → `lodash@^4.17.4` — 2 hops\n4. `webpack` → `eslint-plugin-jsdoc` (`^33.0.0`, devDependency) → `lodash@^4.17.21` — 2 hops\n5. `webpack` → `eslint-plugin-jest` (`^24.3.6`, devDependency) → `@typescript-eslint/experimental-utils@^4.0.1` → `@typescript-eslint/typescript-estree@4.8.2` → `lodash@^4.17.15` — 3 hops\n6. `webpack` → `tooling` (`webpack/tooling#v1.20.0`, devDependency) → `json-schema-to-typescript@^9.1.1` → `lodash@^4.17.15` — 3 hops\n7. `webpack` → `jest` / `jest-cli` (`^27.3.1`, devDependencies — the **npm-published** jest v27, distinct from the `/workspace/jest` v29.0.0 repo analyzed separately in this report) → `jest-environment-jsdom@^27.3.1` → `jsdom@^16.6.0` → `whatwg-url@^8.5.0` → `lodash@^4.7.0` — 5 hops\n\n### jest (`/workspace/jest/`)\n\nTraced via root `/workspace/jest/yarn.lock` (yarn berry lockfile):\n\n1. `@jest/monorepo` (root) → `@babel/core@7.12.9` (pinned exact version, root-level tooling/devDependency chain) → `lodash@^4.17.19` — 2 hops\n2. `/workspace/jest/website/package.json` (docusaurus site; not a declared workspace member but resolved against the root lockfile since it has no lockfile of its own) → `@docusaurus/core@2.0.1` → `lodash@^4.17.21` — 2 hops\n3. `/workspace/jest/examples/manual-mocks/package.json` → `lodash@^4.17.19` — 1 hop, direct, but **unpinned** (no lockfile covers this standalone example)\n\nNumerous other e2e fixture directories (`/workspace/jest/e2e/*/yarn.lock`, e.g. `global-setup`, `global-teardown`, `async-regenerator`, `native-esm`, `babel-plugin-jest-hoist`, `transform/*`) pull in `lodash.debounce`, `lodash.snakecase`, and `lodash.uniqwith` — these are separate, single-function npm packages (not the main `lodash` package) via `@parcel/watcher`/`cosmiconfig`-style dependency chains, and are **out of scope for CVE-2021-23337**, which only affects the `_.template` function shipped in the main `lodash` package.\n\n## 4. Version Analysis\n\n| Consumer | Resolved lodash version | In vulnerable range (`<4.17.21`)? |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/lodash` (the package itself) | 4.17.20 | **Yes — vulnerable** |\n| `/workspace/webpack` (all paths in §3.1–3.7, hoisted by yarn v1) | 4.17.21 | No — patched |\n| `/workspace/webpack` `lodash-es` | 4.17.21 | No — patched (and `lodash-es` is out of CVE-2021-23337's advisory scope regardless) |\n| `/workspace/jest` root workspace / `@babel/core@7.12.9` path | 4.17.21 | No — patched |\n| `/workspace/jest/website` (docusaurus) | 4.17.21 | No — patched |\n| `/workspace/jest/examples/manual-mocks` | **Unresolved — no lockfile** | Indeterminate; range `^4.17.19` permits 4.17.21, so a fresh install today pulls the patched version, but there is no lockfile pinning it, so this manifest offers no protection against a downgrade/older cached install |\n\n### Summary\n\n- The **only confirmed live instance of the vulnerable lodash code** in this workspace is `/workspace/lodash` itself, pinned at 4.17.20.\n- Both **webpack** and the **jest** monorepo pull in many transitive requests for `lodash` (ranging from `^4.7.0` to `^4.17.21`), but in every case their respective yarn lockfiles deduplicate/hoist all of those requests to a single resolved version, **4.17.21**, which is already patched. None of the direct or transitive paths in webpack or jest's own lockfiles resolve to a vulnerable version.\n- The one manifest with a direct dependency and **no lockfile** — `/workspace/jest/examples/manual-mocks/package.json` — is not part of the jest workspace/build and is not enforced by any committed lockfile, so it is a hygiene gap worth flagging even though its semver range would currently resolve to the patched version.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":88199,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":67,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e06e7dab-aaf5-4d86-8da5-13e064348fdc","uuid":"78f2b7c6-c709-4f2b-bc9f-01c9b6a1af61","timestamp":"2026-07-29T14:37:19.069Z","request_id":"req_011CdWWyd7Nn2cNnh3beMe9f"}
