ng/devDependency chain) → `lodash@^4.17.19` — 2 hops\n2. `/workspace/jest/website/package.json` (docusaurus site; not a declared workspace member but resolved against the root lockfile since it has no lockfile of its own) → `@docusaurus/core@2.0.1` → `lodash@^4.17.21` — 2 hops\n3. `/workspace/jest/examples/manual-mocks/package.json` → `lodash@^4.17.19` — 1 hop, direct, but **unpinned** (no lockfile covers this standalone example)\n\nNumerous other e2e fixture directories (`/workspace/jest/e2e/*/yarn.lock`, e.g. `global-setup`, `global-teardown`, `async-regenerator`, `native-esm`, `babel-plugin-jest-hoist`, `transform/*`) pull in `lodash.debounce`, `lodash.snakecase`, and `lodash.uniqwith` — these are separate, single-function npm packages (not the main `lodash` package) via `@parcel/watcher`/`cosmiconfig`-style dependency chains, and are **out of scope for CVE-2021-23337**, which only affects the `_.template` function shipped in the main `lodash` package.\n\n## 4. Version Analysis\n\n| Consumer | Resolved lodash version | In vulnerable range (`<4.17.21`)? |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/lodash` (the package itself) | 4.17.20 | **Yes — vulnerable** |\n| `/workspace/webpack` (all paths in §3.1–3.7, hoisted by yarn v1) | 4.17.21 | No — patched |\n| `/workspace/webpack` `lodash-es` | 4.17.21 | No — patched (and `lodash-es` is out of CVE-2021-23337's advisory scope regardless) |\n| `/workspace/jest` root workspace / `@babel/core@7.12.9` path | 4.17.21 | No — patched |\n| `/workspace/jest/website` (docusaurus) | 4.17.21 | No — patched |\n| `/workspace/jest/examples/manual-mocks` | **Unresolved — no lockfile** | Indeterminate; range `^4.17.19` permits 4.17.21, so a fresh install today pulls the patched version, but there is no lockfile pinning it, so this manifest offers no protection against a downgrade/older cached install |\n\n### Summary\n\n- The **only confirmed live instance of the vulnerable lodash code** in this workspace is `/workspace/lodash` itself, pinned at 4.